From 9f6a9392b9e530df8b7ede81ca6795d2884c2362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anthonybartczak <to0oni456@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:15:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Acknowledge the events channel so notifications keep flowing

An HX Effects (firmware 3.80) stops sending notifications after 195 of
them and stays silent, across new sessions, until its power is pulled.
`tonepush watch` alone reproduces it: power cycle, touch nothing, and
the ticks stop after about 35 s.

The device sends at most 4 KB of notifications that no ACK frame has
acknowledged (195 ticks of 21 bytes is 4095 bytes). hx-usb only sent
keep-alives on the events channel while idle, which the device does not
count, and `keepalive` then marked the channel acknowledged, so later
requests skipped it too. HX Edit ACKs almost every notification
(mac-library-capture.log: 3453 data frames, 3334 ACKs).

- `poll_notifications` sends an ACK on the events channel whenever it
  is owed bytes. No host transaction runs on that channel, so this
  cannot land mid-transaction.
- `keepalive` no longer marks the events channel acknowledged.
- `fake::Pedal::events_window` models the 4 KB window; the new test
  runs watch's loop for 600 notifications. Without the fix it stops at
  exactly 195.

Measured on an HX Effects at 3.80 with a Raspberry Pi 4, power cycle
before each run, pedal untouched, three minutes: upstream `watch` 195
then silence; with this change 1095, still flowing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
